## Issues

### Active (alignment pass 2026-04-25 — root revision: schema collapse + field rename)

- [x] `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide` description: "applies install-time `${rootPath}` interpolation to `mcpServerConfig.args` only..."
  The interpolation surface still exists for advanced users (the parser still supports `${...}` of frontmatter fields), but `${rootPath}` is no longer a load-bearing case because `rootPath` is removed from the schema. The description should generalize: "frontmatter-value interpolation into args" (any field the user references), with an editorial note that the default scaffold doesn't exercise it.
  Traces to: `.aide/intent.aide` outcomes.desired ("The parser still supports `${...}` interpolation of frontmatter fields inside `mcpServerConfig.args` for advanced users... but that surface is not exercised by the default scaffold").
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide` outcomes.desired (typed frontmatter shape): "Reads `.aide/brain.aide` from disk and returns a structured value with the typed frontmatter object (`connector`, `rootPath`, `entryFile`, `mcpServerConfig`, `tools`)..."
  Five-field schema, every field is wrong: path is now `.aide/config/brain.aide`; the schema is exactly `name` + `mcpServerConfig.{command, args}`; `connector` renamed to `name`; `rootPath`, `entryFile`, `tools` removed entirely. The `BrainAideConfig` shape exported from `src/types/index.ts` needs to collapse to the two-field shape, and the parser needs to reject (with `malformed-frontmatter`) any of the removed fields.
  Traces to: `.aide/intent.aide` outcomes.desired ("`brain.aide`'s frontmatter contains exactly two top-level fields: `name` (string) and `mcpServerConfig` (object with `command` and `args`). No `connector`, no `rootPath`, no `entryFile`, no `tools` — the schema is the minimum that still has real consumers").
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide` outcomes.desired ("Provides an interpolation helper applied at install time only: given the parsed frontmatter, returns a copy of `mcpServerConfig.args` with every `${rootPath}` placeholder substituted with the frontmatter's `rootPath` value"): the helper still exists, but the only frontmatter value the default schema carries is `name`; with `rootPath` removed there is no longer a `${rootPath}` placeholder to substitute. The helper should be reframed as "substitutes any `${fieldName}` against the frontmatter's matching field," with `${name}` being the only currently-resolvable placeholder.
  Traces to: `.aide/intent.aide` outcomes.desired (parser supports `${...}` of frontmatter fields; not exercised by default scaffold).
  Misalignment: spec-gap

- [x] `src/service/parseBrainAide/.aide` outcomes.desired ("Failure to read or parse the file collapses to a structured tagged result"): the three failure shapes (`missing`, `malformed-frontmatter`, `malformed-body`) are still load-bearing. But under the new schema, `malformed-frontmatter` should specifically reject any of the removed fields (`rootPath`, `entryFile`, `tools`, `connector`) as well as missing required fields (`name`, `mcpServerConfig.command`, `mcpServerConfig.args`).
  Traces to: `.aide/intent.aide` outcomes.undesired ("Any frontmatter field added to `brain.aide` whose only consumer is the parser's own validation... is validation theater and is rejected").
